<title>USA: Chateau says in compliance with NYSE.</title>
<headline>Chateau says in compliance with NYSE.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chateau Properties Inc said Friday that it is in compliance with New York Stock Exchange requirements.</p>
<p>&quot;We believe that we are in full compliance with all Exchange requirements. Any claims to the contrary are baseless,&quot; the company said in a press release.</p>
<p>Earlier, Oppenheimer and Co, which owns a seven percent stake in Chateau and under five percent in ROC Communities Inc, said it asked the NYSE to review the merger deal between Chateau and ROC.</p>
<p>Oppenheimer said that actions recently approved by the companies may violate listing requirements and cause the surviving company's stock to be delisted by the exchange.</p>
</text>
